IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vea-veteran`

-- Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 -- my degree of incapacity under the Approved Guide (s 29; Table 23.1), and whether I am
-- permanently incapacitated for work under the Repatriation Commission's s 37AA determination, with the disability pension
-- and invalidity service pension questions asked again from those. A module beside vea-veteran.l4 in the same baseline; it
-- IMPORTs that module and changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the veteran (as in vea-veteran.l4) -- "My impairment rating is 52 and my lifestyle rating 4: what is my degree of
-- incapacity, and what rate of pension does that give me? Am I permanently incapacitated for work for the invalidity service
-- pension?"
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, compilation C2026C00275, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03268.txt, ss 21A, 22, 29, 37, 37AA;
--   the Guide to the Assessment of Rates of Veterans' Pensions (No. 2) 2016 (F2016L01332), the Approved Guide under s 29, as
--   deposited at ../../../guide-to-the-assessment-of-rates-of-veterans-pensions-no-2-2016/registers/source-bundle/F2016L01332.txt,
--   with Table 23.1 transcribed in F2016L01332.tables.md beside it (the text conversion lost the table's cells);
--   the Veterans' Entitlements (Invalidity Service Pension - Permanent Incapacity for Work) Determination 2023 (F2023L01239), as
--   deposited at ../../../veterans-entitlements-invalidity-service-pension-permanent-incapacity-for-work-determination-2023/
--   registers/source-bundle/F2023L01239.txt.
--
-- NOT HERE. The impairment ratings themselves (the Guide's Chapters 1-17 and the Combined Values Chart, Table 18.1) and the
-- lifestyle rating (Chapter 22) are the Commission's assessment: asked as facts. Table 24.1 (minimum degrees for listed
-- disabilities) is not encoded (NOTES.md finding 12). The rates in force after indexation are still inputs: the s 198
-- indexation formulas are lost from the Act's deposit and DVA's published rates could not be fetched (NOTES.md finding 13).

§ `The Approved Guide and the s 37AA determination -- my degree of incapacity and my capacity for work`

§§ `Guide Chapters 18 and 23 -- my degree of incapacity (if you receive or claimed a disability pension)`

-- Guide, General Principles: "The combined impairment rating obtained by applying Table 18.1 (Combined Values Chart) is to be
-- rounded to the nearest five points. If Table 18.1 is not required to be applied because only one impairment rating has been
-- obtained and that rating is not a multiple of five, that rating is to be rounded to the nearest five points (or to zero) to
-- produce the impairment rating for the purposes of applying Table 23.1 ... and for the purposes of the extreme disablement
-- adjustment." Ratings are whole points, so no rating lies exactly between two multiples of five.
@export What is my impairment rating for Table 23.1 and the extreme disablement adjustment, once my combined impairment rating is rounded to the nearest five points?
GIVEN `my combined impairment rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating in points from all accepted conditions, as the Commission has assessed it under the Approved Guide (before rounding)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my rounded impairment rating` MEANS
    5 TIMES FLOOR ((`my combined impairment rating` PLUS 2.5) DIVIDED BY 5)

-- Guide Chapter 23: "After a Combined Impairment Rating has been obtained and rounded to the nearest 5 points (or to zero), and a
-- Lifestyle Rating has also been obtained, the rounded Combined Impairment Rating and the Lifestyle Rating are to be combined to
-- establish the degree of incapacity ... Apply Table 23.1". Steps 1-3: the row of the impairment rating, the column of the
-- lifestyle rating (0 to 7), "The number at this intersection is the degree of incapacity." Table 23.1 (F2016L01332.tables.md):
-- each row below is one impairment rating, its eight cells for lifestyle ratings 0 to 7; N/A is written -1. Rows 65 to 90 are
-- 100 throughout; the table has no row above 90.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 0` MEANS LIST 0, 10, 10, 20, -1, -1, -1, -1

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 5` MEANS LIST 10, 10, 20, 30, 40, 40, -1, -1

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 10` MEANS LIST 10, 20, 30, 30, 40, 50, 60, -1

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 15` MEANS LIST 20, 30, 30, 40, 50, 60, 60, -1

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 20` MEANS LIST 20, 30, 40, 50, 50, 60, 70, 80

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 25` MEANS LIST 30, 40, 40, 50, 60, 70, 70, 80

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 30` MEANS LIST 40, 40, 50, 60, 70, 70, 80, 80

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 35` MEANS LIST -1, 50, 60, 60, 70, 80, 90, 90

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 40` MEANS LIST -1, 50, 60, 70, 80, 80, 90, 100

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 45` MEANS LIST -1, 60, 70, 80, 80, 90, 100, 100

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 50` MEANS LIST -1, 70, 70, 80, 90, 100, 100, 100

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 55` MEANS LIST -1, 70, 80, 90, 90, 100, 100, 100

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1 row 60` MEANS LIST -1, 80, 90, 90, 100, 100, 100, 100

GIVETH A LIST OF LIST OF NUMBER
`Table 23.1, impairment 0 to 60` MEANS LIST `Table 23.1 row 0`, `Table 23.1 row 5`, `Table 23.1 row 10`, `Table 23.1 row 15`, `Table 23.1 row 20`, `Table 23.1 row 25`, `Table 23.1 row 30`, `Table 23.1 row 35`, `Table 23.1 row 40`, `Table 23.1 row 45`, `Table 23.1 row 50`, `Table 23.1 row 55`, `Table 23.1 row 60`

DECLARE `My degree of incapacity under Table 23.1` IS ONE OF
    `my degree of incapacity is` HAS `the percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `Table 23.1 gives no degree for that impairment and lifestyle rating (N/A): the lifestyle rating is not one the Guide allows with that impairment rating`
    `not covered: Table 23.1 has no row for an impairment rating above 90, or the lifestyle rating is not 0 to 7`

@export What is my degree of incapacity under Table 23.1 of the Approved Guide, from my impairment and lifestyle ratings?
GIVEN `my combined impairment rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating in points from all accepted conditions, as the Commission has assessed it under the Approved Guide (before rounding)
      `my lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating (0 to 7) under Chapter 22 of the Approved Guide
GIVETH A `My degree of incapacity under Table 23.1`
`What is my degree of incapacity under Table 23.1` MEANS
    IF `the row` GREATER THAN 90 OR `my lifestyle rating` LESS THAN 0 OR `my lifestyle rating` GREATER THAN 7
    THEN `not covered: Table 23.1 has no row for an impairment rating above 90, or the lifestyle rating is not 0 to 7`
    ELSE IF `the row` AT LEAST 65
         THEN `my degree of incapacity is` 100
         ELSE IF `the cell` LESS THAN 0
              THEN `Table 23.1 gives no degree for that impairment and lifestyle rating (N/A): the lifestyle rating is not one the Guide allows with that impairment rating`
              ELSE `my degree of incapacity is` `the cell`
    WHERE
        `the row` MEANS `What is my rounded impairment rating` `my combined impairment rating`
        `the cell` MEANS at (at `Table 23.1, impairment 0 to 60` (`the row` DIVIDED BY 5)) `my lifestyle rating`

-- ss 22, 23, 24 from the ratings. vea-veteran.l4's question takes the degree of incapacity and the impairment and lifestyle
-- points as facts; here the degree comes from Table 23.1 and the impairment points are the rounded rating (which the Guide
-- uses "for the purposes of the extreme disablement adjustment", s 22(4)(c)). The indexed rates are still inputs.
DECLARE `My rate of disability pension from my ratings` IS ONE OF
    `my rate is` HAS `the rate` IS A `My rate of disability pension`
    `no degree of incapacity: Table 23.1 gives none for these ratings (N/A), or they are outside the table`

@export What rate of disability pension am I paid, with my degree of incapacity worked out from my ratings under the Approved Guide (ss 22, 23, 24)?
GIVEN `my combined impairment rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating in points from all accepted conditions, as the Commission has assessed it under the Approved Guide (before rounding)
      `my lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating (0 to 7) under Chapter 22 of the Approved Guide
      `I am blinded in both eyes by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been blinded in both eyes as a result of war-caused injury or disease
      `how much I can work` IS A `How much I can work` @desc How much remunerative work your war-caused incapacity alone leaves you able to do
      `it stopped my work and I lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your war-caused incapacity alone stopped you continuing the paid work you were doing, so that you lost earnings (or, under 65 and not working, you were genuinely seeking work and it is the substantial cause of not getting it)
      `I claimed before turning 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the claim (or application for increase) before you turned 65
      `my last job was after 65 after 10 years' work begun before 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claimed at 65 or over: whether your last paid work was after you turned 65, and when it stopped you had worked continuously for at least 10 years starting before 65
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age now, in years
      `the general rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The general rate of disability pension per fortnight as indexed (s 22(3) prints $338.94)
      `the EDA rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The extreme disablement adjustment rate per fortnight as indexed (s 22(4) prints $510.40)
      `the intermediate rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The intermediate rate per fortnight as indexed (s 23(4) prints $619.80)
      `the special rate in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The special (TPI) rate per fortnight as indexed (s 24(4) prints $1,595.66)
GIVETH A `My rate of disability pension from my ratings`
`What rate of disability pension do my ratings give me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is my degree of incapacity under Table 23.1` `my combined impairment rating` `my lifestyle rating`
    WHEN `my degree of incapacity is` `p` THEN
        `my rate is` (`What rate of disability pension am I paid` `p` `I am blinded in both eyes by it` `how much I can work` `it stopped my work and I lost earnings` `I claimed before turning 65` `my last job was after 65 after 10 years' work begun before 65` `my age` (`What is my rounded impairment rating` `my combined impairment rating`) `my lifestyle rating` `the general rate in force` `the EDA rate in force` `the intermediate rate in force` `the special rate in force`)
    OTHERWISE `no degree of incapacity: Table 23.1 gives none for these ratings (N/A), or they are outside the table`

§§ `s 37AA determination -- am I permanently incapacitated for work (if you are claiming the invalidity service pension)`

-- Act s 37(1)(c): eligible if the veteran "is permanently incapacitated for work in accordance with a determination under
-- section 37AA". Determination 2023 s 7: "a person is permanently incapacitated for work if: at least one of the following
-- applies to the person: (i) the person is permanently blind in both eyes; (ii) the person receives a special rate of pension
-- under section 24 of the Act; (iii) the person receives a Special Rate Disability Pension; (iv) the person would receive a
-- Special Rate Disability Pension but for the application of section 204 or section 415 or both of the MRCA to the person; (v)
-- the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission is satisfied the person meets the eligibility criteria mentioned in
-- subsection 199(1) of the MRCA; or (b) all of the following are met: (i) the person has an impairment that, if it was an
-- injury or disease for the Approved Guide ..., would result in a combined impairment rating of 40 or more under Table 18.1 of
-- the Guide; (ii) because of the impairment, the person is permanently unable to work for more than 8 hours a week; (iii) the
-- Commission is satisfied that the impairment is permanent." (The deposit has lost the label "(a)" of the first limb.)
-- s 6: a person permanently incapacitated under the 2013 Determination just before 15 September 2023 is taken to be so under
-- this one.
DECLARE `Why I am, or am not, permanently incapacitated for work` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am permanently incapacitated for work under s 7(a) of the 2023 Determination (blindness, the special rate, an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, or the MRCC's s 199(1) satisfaction)`
    `yes: I am permanently incapacitated for work under s 7(b) of the 2023 Determination (an impairment rated 40 or more that permanently stops me working more than 8 hours a week)`
    `yes: I was permanently incapacitated for work under the 2013 Determination, so I am taken to be under the 2023 Determination (s 6)`
    `no: none of the circumstances in s 7 of the 2023 Determination applies to me`

@export Am I permanently incapacitated for work under the Repatriation Commission's s 37AA determination (for the invalidity service pension)?
GIVEN `I am permanently blind in both eyes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permanently blind in both eyes
      `I receive the special rate under s 24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the special (TPI) rate of disability pension under s 24 of the Veterans' Entitlements Act
      `I receive an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Special Rate Disability Pension under the MRCA, or would but for MRCA s 204 or s 415
      `the MRCC is satisfied I meet MRCA s 199(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission is satisfied that you meet the eligibility criteria in s 199(1) of the MRCA
      `my impairment would rate 40 or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an impairment that, rated as if it were an injury or disease under the Approved Guide, gives a combined impairment rating of 40 or more under Table 18.1
      `because of it I can never work more than 8 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that impairment, you are permanently unable to work for more than 8 hours a week
      `the Commission is satisfied it is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Repatriation Commission is satisfied that the impairment is permanent
      `I was permanently incapacitated under the 2013 Determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before 15 September 2023, you were permanently incapacitated for work under the 2013 Determination
GIVETH A `Why I am, or am not, permanently incapacitated for work`
`Am I permanently incapacitated for work under the s 37AA determination` MEANS
    IF `I am permanently blind in both eyes` OR `I receive the special rate under s 24` OR `I receive an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` OR `the MRCC is satisfied I meet MRCA s 199(1)`
    THEN `yes: I am permanently incapacitated for work under s 7(a) of the 2023 Determination (blindness, the special rate, an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, or the MRCC's s 199(1) satisfaction)`
    ELSE IF `my impairment would rate 40 or more` AND `because of it I can never work more than 8 hours a week` AND `the Commission is satisfied it is permanent`
         THEN `yes: I am permanently incapacitated for work under s 7(b) of the 2023 Determination (an impairment rated 40 or more that permanently stops me working more than 8 hours a week)`
         ELSE IF `I was permanently incapacitated under the 2013 Determination`
              THEN `yes: I was permanently incapacitated for work under the 2013 Determination, so I am taken to be under the 2023 Determination (s 6)`
              ELSE `no: none of the circumstances in s 7 of the 2023 Determination applies to me`

GIVEN `why` IS A `Why I am, or am not, permanently incapacitated for work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `that makes me permanently incapacitated` IF
    NOT (`why` EQUALS `no: none of the circumstances in s 7 of the 2023 Determination applies to me`)

@export Am I eligible for the invalidity service pension (s 37), with permanent incapacity for work worked out under the s 37AA determination?
GIVEN `I have rendered qualifying service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have rendered qualifying service
      `I am permanently blind in both eyes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permanently blind in both eyes
      `I receive the special rate under s 24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the special (TPI) rate of disability pension under s 24 of the Veterans' Entitlements Act
      `I receive an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a Special Rate Disability Pension under the MRCA, or would but for MRCA s 204 or s 415
      `the MRCC is satisfied I meet MRCA s 199(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission is satisfied that you meet the eligibility criteria in s 199(1) of the MRCA
      `my impairment would rate 40 or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an impairment that, rated under the Approved Guide, gives a combined impairment rating of 40 or more
      `because of it I can never work more than 8 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that impairment, you are permanently unable to work for more than 8 hours a week
      `the Commission is satisfied it is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Repatriation Commission is satisfied that the impairment is permanent
      `I was permanently incapacitated under the 2013 Determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, immediately before 15 September 2023, you were permanently incapacitated for work under the 2013 Determination
      `kind` IS A `What kind of veteran I am` @desc Whether you are an Australian veteran, or a veteran only through a Commonwealth or allied force or as an allied mariner
      `I am a refugee or former refugee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a refugee or former refugee
      `my longest continuous residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your longest single period of Australian residence, in years
      `my total residence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of all your periods of Australian residence, in years
      `my incapacity began here, unprovoked and uncompensated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became permanently incapacitated while an Australian resident, not to obtain a pension, and you have no enforceable claim for adequate compensation for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the invalidity service pension, with s 37AA worked out` IF
    `Am I eligible for the invalidity service pension` `I have rendered qualifying service` (`that makes me permanently incapacitated` (`Am I permanently incapacitated for work under the s 37AA determination` `I am permanently blind in both eyes` `I receive the special rate under s 24` `I receive an MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` `the MRCC is satisfied I meet MRCA s 199(1)` `my impairment would rate 40 or more` `because of it I can never work more than 8 hours a week` `the Commission is satisfied it is permanent` `I was permanently incapacitated under the 2013 Determination`)) `kind` `I am a refugee or former refugee` `my longest continuous residence in years` `my total residence in years` `my incapacity began here, unprovoked and uncompensated`
